"""Edition16 original practice; run once."""
import json,pathlib,random
R=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
assert not (R/'data/2026-09-mcqs.json').exists()
rows='''1~Which correctly interprets the Q1 BoP release?~April–June FY2026–27 CAD was US$4.2 billion, or 0.5% of GDP~The CAD equalled the US$86.1 billion merchandise deficit|The data measured only September transactions|The US$8.1 billion reserve entry represented BoP accumulation~Goods, services and income jointly determine the current account. The primary table and release show reserve depletion, not accumulation; release month differs from the observation period.
1~Why should personal-transfer receipts of US$42.9 billion not be equated with net secondary income of US$40.8 billion?~A gross receipt measure and a net income-balance measure have different coverage~They necessarily represent a statistical error|They are both identical measures of net FDI|Their difference is automatically the merchandise deficit~Gross receipts and a net account balance are distinct. Preserve definitions and do not mix nonreserve financial flows with reserve-inclusive aggregates.
2~Under the inspected FAQ’s general eligible P2M rule effective 15 October, what is MDR on a ₹1 lakh transaction?~₹300~₹400|₹4,000|₹0 on every merchant transaction~The general rate is 0.4% with a ₹300 cap, reached at ₹75,000. This is merchant MDR subject to category/exemption conditions, not a universal consumer or P2P transfer charge.
2~Which remains distinct from a merchant MDR under the reviewed UPI FAQ?~A direct fee on ordinary P2P transfers, which remain free~The merchant acceptance cost on an eligible P2M transaction|Special-category MDR limits|A cap on the general merchant charge~The FAQ separates free payer/P2P use from selective merchant pricing. It prohibits merchant passthrough, but this does not prove that indirect economic incidence through general prices is impossible.
4~Which legal-stage statement is correct about IBBI’s personal-guarantor proposals?~A discussion paper proposes safeguards but is not itself final amended regulations~Every related party already has nil voting rights solely because a paper was published|Publication automatically cancels all guarantees|The proposed valuation rule guarantees full creditor recovery~The paper discusses related-party voting, avoidance transactions, valuation and creditor reasoning. Comments and later regulatory steps must be distinguished from consultation publication.
5~Which is the sound interpretation of the reviewed money-mule timelines?~They are PRS-reviewed draft procedures, not verified final universal release deadlines~They authorise indefinite freezing without notice|They prove every flagged recipient is convicted|They eliminate the need for bank grievance mechanisms~The RBI release confirms a consultation; detailed procedures were not independently read as a final SOP. Suspicion, debit restriction and criminal conviction remain different stages.
6~In the state WMA advisory context, SDF refers to what?~Special Drawing Facility~Standing Deposit Facility in every context|Sovereign Development Fund|State Debt Forgiveness~The same abbreviation can have context-specific meanings. State liquidity support is repayable and distinct from a fiscal grant; the committee’s recommendations were to be examined, not automatically implemented.
7~The Gazette’s ₹25,000 figure is best described as what?~A wage ceiling for the specified Chapter III social-security purpose~A universal minimum monthly salary|A guaranteed ₹25,000 monthly pension|A mandatory flat ₹25,000 employee contribution~The short notification specifies a statutory coverage ceiling and commencement, not every scheme detail. Wage ceiling, contribution rate, basic pay and pension amount are distinct.
8~Which statement correctly distinguishes GEC III targets?~135 GW concerns renewable evacuation capability and 50 GWh concerns storage energy~135 GWh is instantaneous generation and 50 GW is annual storage output|Both figures measure identical quantities|The targets prove all assets were already commissioned on 30 September~Power and energy are different dimensions. Cabinet approval and a target do not establish installed or operating capacity, state allocations or completed spending.
10~When do the reviewed e-commerce amendments commence?~1 January 2027~Immediately on the September notification date|Only after every platform voluntarily agrees|1 April 2027~The inspected Gazette gives 1 January 2027. The separate food-laboratory amendments commence 1 April 2027; legal instruments should not be mixed.
10~What is the inspected price-reference rule for a displayed discount?~The prior price is the lowest price in the preceding 30 days~Any historical maximum chosen by the seller|The average price in the next calendar year|Always the manufacturer’s highest printed price irrespective of actual pricing~A low prior-price reference helps prevent an inflated base price from manufacturing an apparent discount. It must not be replaced with an unspecified notion of old price.
13~Which MSP interpretation is correct for the 30 September decision?~Wheat ₹2,610 per quintal applies to the 2027–28 rabi marketing season~₹2,610 is per tonne for the 2026 kharif season|Every grower is guaranteed unlimited government purchases|The decision itself proves all farmers realised that price~MSP announcement, procurement access and realised prices differ. The official cost footnote uses paid-out costs plus family labour, not automatically C2.
14~What does Acceptance of Necessity establish?~In-principle procurement approval before later contracting and delivery~A completed delivery certificate|An audited payment for all equipment|Proof every subsystem has 98% domestic content~The DAC headline concerns about ₹1.10 lakh crore of proposals. The planned Indian-industry procurement share is not identical to domestic content in every component.
16~Which is correct about the food-laboratory amendment?~It commences 1 April 2027, with different specified timelines for import and regulatory/referral reports~It commenced immediately on 14 September and abolished validated methods|Every food sample has exactly the same five-day deadline|A late report automatically proves the food is safe~The inspected passage distinguishes 14-day regulatory/referral reporting and five-day import reporting, with reasons for delay. Scientific validity and legal procedure remain essential.
18~ULPIN/Bhu-Aadhaar principally identifies what?~A land parcel through a 14-digit identifier~A person’s bank account through 12 digits|A judicially guaranteed title with no right of appeal|A new currency used for stamp duty~Parcel identification can link records, but does not automatically adjudicate title, remove errors or extinguish other rights.
22~Which statement about rare-earth magnets is correct?~Ore availability alone does not establish separation, alloy and magnet-manufacturing capability~Every geological resource is an economically recoverable reserve|A November 2025 scheme is a new September 2026 sanction merely because a magazine revisits it|All rare-earth minerals can be processed without environmental controls~Strategic capability requires the entire value chain. Historical magazine review should not silently change an approval’s date.
23~Which is a central limitation of asset tokenisation?~A digital token does not by itself cure defects in the underlying legal title~A blockchain entry automatically repeals land law|Fractional claims remove every custody and fraud risk|A token automatically authorises public investment solicitation~Off-chain records, legally enforceable claims, custody, redemption, tax and regulatory jurisdiction remain important. Technical settlement does not equal unquestionable ownership.
25~Which is correct about bamboo regulation?~The 2017 change concerns bamboo outside forest areas; forest controls are not universally abolished~All harvesting inside forests became unrestricted|Bamboo is botanically a hardwood tree|Every bamboo plantation is automatically ecologically beneficial~Botanical classification and legal definitions are distinct. Location, rights, species and supply-chain design matter for lawful and sustainable livelihoods.
29~Why does Kigali address HFCs?~Their climate-warming impact, despite their generally not being ozone-depleting substances~They are identical to CFCs in every property|They exclusively cause ground-level ozone and have no climate relevance|Kigali immediately bans all cooling equipment~The Montreal framework and Kigali connect ozone transition with climate protection, but the physical problems and phasedown obligations must be distinguished.
32~Which statement about hanging glaciers is correct?~They can form naturally, while warming and local physical conditions can affect stability~Every hanging glacier is solely a creation of recent climate change|Every ice avalanche is a glacial-lake outburst|Mapped hanging glaciers are necessarily about to collapse~Geometry, slope, fractures and bed conditions influence hazards. An ice avalanche, GLOF and rain-driven flood are different initiating processes that may cascade.
36~Why is the lunar far side of interest for early-universe radio observations?~Lunar shielding can reduce terrestrial radio interference~It is permanently dark and never receives sunlight|It eliminates all instrumental noise and foregrounds|The received high-redshift signal must always remain exactly at 21 cm~The far side receives sunlight. The 21 cm rest transition is redshifted; calibration and foregrounds remain challenges even with radio shielding.
38~Which distinction is scientifically correct?~Typhoid and non-typhoidal Salmonella are not interchangeable disease categories~All Salmonella infections are typhoid|A typhoid vaccine necessarily prevents every Salmonella infection|A typhoid case estimate automatically measures non-typhoidal disease~Different serovars and syndromes require careful interpretation. A study’s case definition and population cannot be silently changed when reporting its burden estimate.
45~What follows from a Cabinet agenda discussion of cage culture?~Site-specific permissions and environmental safeguards still require verification~Every reservoir automatically receives a legal operating licence|Carrying capacity becomes irrelevant|Traditional fisher access is automatically extinguished~A draft policy or discussion is not a site allotment. Water quality, waste, disease, common-water use and participation need explicit safeguards.
47~Which statement about a reported ₹94 crore DBT proposal is defensible?~Eligibility, sanction and actual disbursement must be checked separately~Every tobacco grower has already received an identical payment|DBT means there can be no payment failure|The amount proves every farmer’s income has doubled~DBT describes a payment mechanism, not automatic universal entitlement or an audited receipt. The reviewed news report did not provide original rules or bank-level verification.
50~A proposed ₹950 crore utility guarantee is what?~A contingent obligation distinct from an immediate ₹950 crore grant~An automatic waiver of the utility’s debt|Proof the transmission asset is commissioned|A transaction with no possible fiscal risk~A guarantee may be called if specified obligations fail. Borrowing, disbursement, project operation and actual state payment are different stages and should be disclosed separately.
51~Which preserves the Nellore land decision’s reported scope?~22.31 of 62.70 acres, retaining active-canal/operational exclusions and a reported 20-foot buffer~The entire 62.70 acres including the active canal|Every canal in AP was reclassified|No land survey or flood-risk assessment can be relevant~The reported Cabinet decision has a limited extent. Reclassification is distinct from allotment, possession and safe construction; the original GO and survey were not independently inspected.
52~Which four cities are named in the reviewed commissionerate approval?~Tirupati, Guntur, Kurnool and Rajamahendravaram~Kadapa, Srikakulam, Ongole and Chittoor|Anantapur, Nellore, Eluru and Machilipatnam|Every district headquarters automatically~The 23 September Cabinet report identifies four cities. Approval does not itself establish final boundaries, commencement, staffing or improved crime outcomes.
54~How should the reported 19,739 jobs in AP investment approvals be treated?~Potential employment conditional on implementation~Verified current payroll employment|A guaranteed job entitlement for every applicant|An audited count of permanent government posts~The ₹22,177.84 crore figure is an approval pipeline. Financial closure, construction, production and sustained work must be separately tracked; unreconciled component totals should not be invented.
56~What is the increase from ₹904 crore to ₹1,548.98 crore in the cited CIIP estimate?~₹644.98 crore, approximately 71.35%~₹644.98 crore, exactly 7.135%|₹1,548.98 crore, approximately 171% additional area irrigated|₹904 crore, proving the same amount was wasted~Subtract the baseline and divide the increase by ₹904 crore. Arithmetic does not identify whether escalation reflects scope, delay, prices or inefficiency; original revised estimates are still needed.
58~Which statement correctly preserves AP commodity-intervention stages?~1.20 lakh tonnes of tur dal was requested, not verified as delivered stock~All requested tur dal was already sold to consumers|The ₹35/kg onion intervention automatically controls every private retail price|A 10,000-tonne rice order proves every tonne was purchased and distributed~Requests, orders, procurement, arrival and retail sale are separate stages. Stage and unit errors are serious even when the headline quantity is remembered.'''
positions=[0]*8+[1]*8+[2]*7+[3]*7;random.Random(16092026).shuffle(positions);Q=[]
for i,line in enumerate(rows.splitlines(),1):
 ref,q,correct,other,ex=line.split('~');opts=other.split('|');random.Random(1600+i).shuffle(opts);pos=positions[i-1];opts.insert(pos,correct)
 Q.append(dict(id=f'SEP26-{i:02}',question=q,options=opts,answer=pos,explanation=ex,ref=f'E16-2609-{int(ref):03}'))
assert len(Q)==30
(R/'data/2026-09-mcqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(Q,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
F=[
(2,'Digital payments need a sustainable funding model without weakening inclusion.',[
'Anchor the 15 September official FAQ and future 15 October commencement. Separate eligible merchant MDR from free ordinary payer/P2P use.',
'Explain the general 0.4% rate, ₹300 cap and exemptions/special categories without applying them indiscriminately to credit-linked products.',
'Analyse resilience, acceptance costs, merchant categorisation, pass-through incentives, competition and small-business margins. No-surcharge rules do not prove indirect economic incidence is impossible.',
'Propose transparent pricing, assisted classification, complaint resolution, reliable infrastructure and review using actual transaction/merchant outcomes.',
'For AP small merchants, test whether compliance knowledge, access and payment reliability improve rather than equating digital transaction growth with universal inclusion.'
]),
(8,'Renewable expansion is a system-integration challenge, not just a generation target.',[
'Anchor GEC III approval on 30 September: headline ₹1,86,405 crore, central support ₹54,082 crore, up to 135 GW evacuation and 50 GWh BESS through FY2032–33.',
'Distinguish power, stored energy, annual output, grid connection and operating service. Withhold unreconciled component sums rather than manufacturing precision.',
'Analyse transmission congestion, right-of-way, variable output, storage duration, degradation, safety and cost allocation.',
'Propose coordinated resource planning, competitive procurement where applicable, transparent milestones and performance monitoring tied to reliability and usable renewables.',
'For AP, link DISCOM finances, industrial/agricultural demand and project pipelines without asserting a new state allocation or already commissioned corridor.'
]),
(10,'Digital-market consumer protection requires enforceable design standards and informed choice.',[
'Anchor the 9 September notification and 1 January 2027 commencement; contrast notification with operative effect.',
'Explain sponsored-ranking transparency, the lowest-prior-30-day discount reference and annual dark-pattern audit requirements.',
'Analyse information asymmetry, platform power, conflicted ranking, seller dependence, complaint evidence and audit credibility.',
'Propose independent enforcement capability, clear disclosures, accessible redress and proportionate sanctions while preserving genuine innovation and small-seller access.',
'For AP, assess whether consumer complaints and seller experiences improve; avoid assuming every online offer is unlawful or every self-audit is reliable.'
]),
(18,'Integrated land information must be accurate, contestable and inclusive.',[
'Anchor DILRMP 3.0’s September roadmap and primary anticipated ₹565.50 crore national outlay, retaining the prelaunch versus launch distinction.',
'Distinguish a 14-digit parcel identifier, map, mutation, registered transaction and adjudicated title; digitisation is not automatic conclusive ownership.',
'Analyse legacy discrepancies, survey quality, interdepartmental responsibility, privacy, exclusion and access barriers for women, tenants and customary users.',
'Propose notices, assisted claims, ground verification, audit trails, time-bound correction and meaningful appeal alongside interoperable technology.',
'For AP, measure fewer erroneous refusals, resolved disputes and reduced citizen burden rather than only map uploads or assuming a separate newly verified state scheme.'
]),
(35,'Public institutions deploying AI agents must remain accountable for consequential actions.',[
'Anchor the magazine’s selected agentic-AI discussion without presenting simulations as verified incident rates or an industry proposal as a public regulator.',
'Explain the interaction of tool permissions, autonomy, model capability and deployment context. Separate assistive output from actions affecting rights, money or services.',
'Analyse privacy, prompt injection, goal misalignment, unreviewed tool use and unequal capacity to contest automated decisions.',
'Propose least privilege, sandboxing, human approval at consequential boundaries, independent tests, logs, rollback and incident reporting.',
'For AP services, retain human responsibility and accessible appeals; evaluate real service and safety outcomes rather than vendor claims or automation volume.'
]),
(51,'Housing on reclassified public land must protect water infrastructure and disaster safety.',[
'Anchor the reported 3 September Nellore decision: 22.31 of 62.70 acres, active-canal/operational exclusions and reported 20-foot buffer.',
'Distinguish Cabinet approval, revenue reclassification, individual allotment, possession and safe construction; original survey and GO remain unread.',
'Analyse flood pathways, drainage, maintenance access, vulnerable households, boundary accuracy and possible competing public uses.',
'Propose transparent maps, site-specific hazard review, safeguarded access, consultation and grievance correction before irrevocable development.',
'For AP, reconcile housing inclusion with functioning public infrastructure. Do not assume a reported fixed buffer is scientifically sufficient for every location.'
]),
(53,'Government influencer outreach requires public-value safeguards, not merely digital reach.',[
'Anchor AP Cabinet policy reporting on 23 September, with one-year empanelment and conditional annual extensions, not verified executed contracts or payment rates.',
'Distinguish public information, advertising, political campaigning and independent creator speech; explain why paid sponsorship should be visible.',
'Analyse opaque selection, inflated metrics, misinformation risk, public spending, neutrality and chilling of legitimate criticism.',
'Propose transparent criteria, sponsorship labels, records, fact-checking, proportional grievance procedures and independent audit of contracts and outcomes.',
'Measure verified service awareness and uptake, not only views; respect criticism and avoid equating government disagreement with misinformation.'
]),
(54,'State investment policy should reward realised public value rather than approval totals.',[
'Anchor the reported ₹22,177.84 crore AP pipeline and 19,739 potential jobs; retain projected, not realised, status.',
'Map approval, land/clearances, financial closure, construction, production and sustained payroll. Do not invent a reconciled sector breakdown from conflicting numbers.',
'Analyse infrastructure, water and energy demand, environmental capacity, skill fit, regional distribution, incentive costs and contingent fiscal exposure.',
'Propose project-level dashboards, milestone-based support, transparent conditions, lawful clawbacks, worker safeguards and independently checked performance.',
'Conclude with realised investment, durable quality jobs and net public benefit; neither MoUs nor capital-per-projected-job ratios alone establish success.'
])]
N={n['id']:n for n in json.loads((R/'data/notes.json').read_text())};out=['# September 2026 · Original Mains answer frameworks','','Eight frameworks for 150/250-word practice; not model claims of current law or exhaustive coverage. Preserve consultation and implementation stages.','']
for i,(ref,prompt,points)in enumerate(F,1):
 key=f'E16-2609-{ref:03}';out += [f'## {i}. {prompt}',f'Study anchor: {key} · {N[key]["title"]}','']+[f'{j}. {x}'for j,x in enumerate(points,1)]+['']
(R/'volumes/September-2026-Mains-Frameworks.md').write_text('\n'.join(out)+'\n')
print('Authored 30 MCQs; answer distribution', {chr(65+i):positions.count(i)for i in range(4)},'; 8 Mains frameworks')
